@startuml

' =============================================================
' UC-005 System Sequence Diagram (PIM) - English
'
' MDA Level: Platform Independent Model
' Perspective: Specification / Analysis
'
' Derived from PIM use case by applying mapping rule M2 (Goal -> Use Case)
' and M4 (Implicit Knowledge -> Explicit System Behavior).
'
' Compare with: uc-005.usecase.pim.md
'
' This SSD shows the system as a BLACK BOX. We see only:
' - Actors
' - Messages crossing the system boundary
' - System responses
'
' We do NOT see internal classes, services, or implementation.
' Those appear in the PSM Sequence Diagram.
'
' Notice: No HTTP, no JSON, no REST, no SQL. Messages are
' abstract system operations. Parameters use PIM types only.
' =============================================================

title UC-005 System Sequence Diagram — Phone List Coordination (PIM)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #4682B4
skinparam sequenceBoxBorderColor #4682B4

actor "Caregiver" as Caregiver
participant "Phone Coordination\nSystem" as System <<system>>
actor "System Time Event" as TimeEvent

== View Phone List for Active Shift ==

Caregiver -> System : getPhoneListForActiveShift()
activate System
System --> Caregiver : phoneList : List<PhoneAssignment>
deactivate System

== Assign Caregiver Name to Phone ==

Caregiver -> System : selectShift(shiftType : ShiftType)
activate System
System --> Caregiver : phoneList : List<PhoneAssignment>
deactivate System

Caregiver -> System : assignPhone(phoneNumber : String,\ncaregiverName : String,\nshiftType : ShiftType)
activate System

alt assignment valid
    System --> Caregiver : assignmentConfirmed : PhoneAssignment
else shift not selected (Rule M5)
    System --> Caregiver : error : ShiftTypeRequired
else business rule violation (Rule M5)
    System --> Caregiver : error : RuleViolation
else persistence failed
    System --> Caregiver : error : PersistenceFailed
end

deactivate System

== Clear Assignment ==

Caregiver -> System : clearAssignment(phoneNumber : String,\nshiftType : ShiftType)
activate System
System --> Caregiver : clearConfirmed
deactivate System

== Automatic Refresh (Time-Triggered) ==

TimeEvent -> System : refreshPhoneList()
activate System
System --> TimeEvent : phoneList : List<PhoneAssignment>
deactivate System

note over System
    <b>System as black box (PIM-level):</b>

    The system's internal structure is NOT shown here.
    No services, no managers, no repositories.
    Those concerns are PSM (platform-specific).

    <b>Message types are PIM-generic:</b>
    - String, ShiftType, List<T> — platform-independent
    - NO HTTP, NO JSON, NO REST verbs
    - NO async/Task — those are platform constructs

    <b>System Time Event is an internal actor (Rule M1):</b>
    It represents the system's capability to react to time.
    In CIM there is no such actor.
end note

@enduml
